%# expected-result: FAIL
%description:
Expected failure by explicit maintainer decision: defer this nontrivial repair to future work.
Repair requires noncontiguous channel representation and end-to-end PHY observation; the current explicit testability assertion must also be replaced.
Evidence and deferred-repair decision: doc/project/evidence/model/wifi/results.md#deferred-repair-expectations.
This declaration records unresolved work, not supported behavior.

Testability gap: No two-segment channel representation is exposed by the VHT mode API; bandwidth alone cannot establish 80+80 MHz.
The failure is an explicit missing observation, not proof that an emitted frame is wrong.

%file: Ac_80p80.cc

#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "WifiTestSupport.h"

namespace inet {
namespace protocoltest {

using namespace inet::units::values;

Define_ProtocolTest(wifi_11ac_80p80)
{
    return ProtocolTest("wifi_11ac_80p80")
        .once(on("sta1.wlan[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("ieee80211mac.type == 40")
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext&) -> bool {
                      throw cRuntimeError("TESTABILITY GAP: No two-segment channel representation is exposed by the VHT mode API; bandwidth alone cannot establish 80+80 MHz");
                  })
                  .describe("a VHT data frame using 80+80 MHz non-contiguous channel")
                  .within(2.5));
}

} // namespace protocoltest
} // namespace inet

%inifile: test.ini

[General]
*.tester.testName = "wifi_11ac_80p80"
include ../../ini/_ac.ini
include ../../ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST wifi_11ac_80p80: PASS
